{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q419693","formula":"C₆H₁₀CaO₆","hill":"C6H10CaO6","elements":["H","C","O","Ca"],"composition":{"C":6.0,"H":10.0,"O":6.0,"Ca":1.0},"names":{"en":"Calcium DL-lactate","ru":"Лактат кальция"},"descriptions":{"en":"Calcium lactate is a white crystalline salt with formula C6H10CaO6, consisting of two lactate anions H3C(CHOH)CO2– for each calcium cation Ca2+. It forms several hydrates, the most common being the pentahydrate C6H10CaO6·5H2O. Calcium lactate is used in medicine, mainly to treat calcium deficiencies; and as a food additive with E number of E327. Some cheese crystals consist of calcium lactate.","ru":"Лакта́т ка́льция — кальциевая соль молочной кислоты (кальций молочнокислый). Используется в пищевой промышленности в качестве пищевой добавки Е327 как регулятор кислотности, влагоудерживающий агент, эмульгирующая соль, синергист антиоксидантов."},"fame":22,"pubchemCid":13144,"mass":218.22,"charge":0,"smiles":"CC(C(=O)[O-])O.CC(C(=O)[O-])O.[Ca+2]","inchikey":"MKJXYGKVIBWPFZ-UHFFFAOYSA-L","iupac":"calcium bis(2-hydroxypropanoate)","classes":[{"qid":"Q59199015","names":{"en":"group of stereoisomers","ru":"группа стереоизомеров","uk":"група стереоізомерів"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"rdkit","ref":"13144","atoms":23,"license":"Computed with RDKit from SMILES (PubChem, Wikidata)"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":-1.478,"y":-2.227,"z":-1.45,"el":"C"},{"x":-0.109,"y":-1.581,"z":-1.489,"el":"C"},{"x":0.722,"y":-1.91,"z":-0.211,"el":"C"},{"x":1.188,"y":-0.872,"z":0.36,"el":"O"},{"x":0.841,"y":-3.128,"z":0.091,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.277,"y":-0.145,"z":-1.598,"el":"O"},{"x":-2.07,"y":-1.928,"z":-2.321,"el":"H"},{"x":-1.408,"y":-3.319,"z":-1.434,"el":"H"},{"x":-2.034,"y":-1.907,"z":-0.562,"el":"H"},{"x":0.452,"y":-1.911,"z":-2.369,"el":"H"},{"x":0.29,"y":0.174,"z":-0.852,"el":"H"},{"x":-0.872,"y":1.692,"z":0.668,"el":"C"},{"x":0.497,"y":2.338,"z":0.629,"el":"C"},{"x":1.328,"y":2.009,"z":1.907,"el":"C"},{"x":1.794,"y